  "tapeHelp1": "Allow the camera, then move the phone slowly over a table, floor or wall until white dots appear and the aim sits on the surface.",
  "tapeHelp2": "Aim the crosshair at a corner and tap Add point. Move to the next corner: the length follows the aim.",
  "tapeHelp3": "Keep tapping corners to chain pieces; the panel adds them up. Aim back at the first point and tap Close shape for the area and perimeter.",
  "tapeHelp4": "Undo takes the last point away (or opens a closed shape); Clear starts again. The button at the top switches between centimetres and inches.",
  "tapeTip": "AR measuring is approximate: often within 1 to 3 cm over a metre, but worse on plain or shiny surfaces, in dim light, far away (over 3 m) or when the phone moves fast. Move slowly and keep the corners in good light. The picture is never recorded, saved or sent."
